# Design System Rules

**Source of truth:** `packages/design-system/`. Import via `@rotate/design-system/design-system.css` in layouts only. Components do not import CSS directly.

**Rule index:** `.cursor/rules/README.md`.

---

## Breakpoints (critical)

**Do NOT use `md:` or `lg:`.** This project uses custom breakpoint names.

| Tailwind variant | Value | Use for |
|------------------|-------|---------|
| `tablet:` | 768px | `min-width: 768px` |
| `desktop:` | 1024px | `min-width: 1024px` |

- **Correct:** `tablet:flex`, `desktop:grid-cols-3`, `tablet:px-[var(--grid-default-margin)]`
- **Wrong:** `md:flex`, `lg:grid-cols-3`, `sm:px-4`

In raw CSS: `@media (min-width: theme(--breakpoint-tablet))` or `theme(--breakpoint-desktop)`.

---

## Colors

Use semantic tokens. **Prefer utility classes** when Tailwind generates them from `--color-*`:
- `bg-background-default-primary`, `bg-background-default-primary-lightest`, `text-content-default-primary`, `border-border-default-primary`, etc.
- Format: `{utility}-{key}` from `--color-{key}` (e.g. `--color-content-default-primary` → `text-content-default-primary`).

Fall back to arbitrary values when no utility exists: `bg-[var(--color-background-default-primary)]`. Do not hardcode hex values.

**Theming:** Root uses `data-theme="light"` or `data-theme="dark"`. Colors use `light-dark()` for automatic switching.

---

## Typography

Use `@utility` classes from design-system. Do not hardcode font-size, font-family, or letter-spacing.

**Title styles:** `title-style1-*` … `title-style4-*` (100–1000)  
**Body styles:** `body-style1-*` … `body-style3-*` (100–1000)  
**Longform:** `longform-style1-*` (100–1000)  
**Thumbnails:** `thumbnail-title`, `thumbnail-description`

Example: `title-style1-600`, `body-style1-400`, `longform-style1-500`.

---

## Spacing

Use `--spacing-*` (0, 25, 50, 75, 100–1300) or `--spacer-spacer-*` (100–800).

**Prefer utility classes** when Tailwind generates them: `p-200`, `gap-300`, `mb-100`, etc. (format: `p-{key}` from `--spacing-{key}`). Fall back to arbitrary values when no utility exists: `p-[var(--spacing-200)]`.

---

## Grid

- **Gutter:** `--grid-default-gutter`, `--grid-fullwidth-gutter`
- **Margin:** `--grid-default-margin`, `--grid-default-margin-offset`
- **Layout:** `grid-cols-12`, `gap-x-[var(--grid-default-gutter)]`, `px-[var(--grid-default-margin)]`
- **Colspans:** `--grid-default-colspan-1` … `--grid-default-colspan-12`, `--grid-default-colspan-fullwidth`

---

## Radius

**Prefer utility classes:** `rounded-radius-primary-smallest`, `rounded-radius-primary-small`, etc. (from `--radius-*`).

- **Primary:** `--radius-radius-primary`, `--radius-radius-primary-smallest` (4px), `--radius-radius-primary-small` (8px), `--radius-radius-primary-large` (16px), `--radius-radius-primary-largest` (32px)
- **Button:** `--radius-radius-button-100` … `--radius-radius-button-400` (all 999px)
- **Full:** `--radius-radius-full` (999px)

---

## Opacity

`--opacity-opacity-0` … `--opacity-opacity-1000` (0–1).

---

## Icons

**Source:** `packages/design-system/src/icon.css` (`@utility icon`, `icon-stroke`, `[data-icon-size]`).

### Scale (set on a **parent** of the SVG)

| `data-icon-size` | `--icon-dimension-width` / `height` (typical) |
|------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| `100` | 16px |
| `200` | 20px |
| `300` | 24px |
| `400` | 32px |

`:root` defaults to **20px** if no `data-icon-size` is set (same as `200`).

### Inline / decorative SVG

1. Put **`data-icon-size="100"` … `"400"`** on the **nearest ancestor** that should own the scale (often the `<a>`, `<button>`, or a wrapper).
2. On the **`<svg>`**, use **`class="icon"`** so width/height resolve from `--icon-dimension-*`.

### Icon-only control (button, toggle) — **no arbitrary `size-[Npx]`**

Spacing tokens (`h-200` = 16px, `h-300` = 24px) **do not** cover every icon pixel size (e.g. **20px**). **Do not** invent `size-[20px]`, `h-[20px]`, etc.

**Do this instead:**

- Set **`data-icon-size="200"`** (or `100` / `300` / `400` per Figma) on the **same element** that needs the hit box (or its wrapper).
- Size the control with **`size-[var(--icon-dimension-width)]`** (square) or **`h-[var(--icon-dimension-height)] w-[var(--icon-dimension-width)]`** so it tracks the icon tokens.
- Put **`class="size-full"`** (or equivalent) on the inner `<svg>` if it should fill that box; keep **`viewBox`** as authored — **viewBox is vector geometry, not a layout token** and may be 20×20 while the control still uses vars.

**Example (menu toggle):** `data-icon-size="200"` + `size-[var(--icon-dimension-width)]` + `inline-flex items-center justify-center` — not `size-[20px]`.

### Stroke icons

- **`icon-stroke`** on stroke-based SVGs for `stroke-width` from `--icon-weight-*`.

### Buttons that include an icon

Prefer **`btn btn-icon`** (and `btn-icon-padded` when Figma shows header-style padding). Set **`data-icon-size`** on the control so the inner **`icon`** SVG matches; avoid duplicating pixel sizes outside `icon.css`.

